§ `A1: Ministry of Education 5 study units for a grade 2 licence (SCH2-B1b)`

-- Second Schedule Part B item 1, column B (2): "a final certificate evidencing climate-control studies at the
-- level of 5 study units (specialisation) from the Ministry of Education" is ITSELF a way of meeting item 1, with
-- nothing further.  Part B item 5, column A (3), lists the same certificate as prior training that needs "training
-- of up to 50 hours" more.  Reading 1 (ind-a's, asserted): the certificate suffices (item 1(2)); reading 2 (the
-- encoding's): item 5 governs because item 1 is for those with no prior training.  The discriminating case: an
-- adult citizen holding only that certificate, no further training, applying for grade 2.
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a application` (`ind-a applicant holding` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units`)) `grade 2 licence` (YMD 2026 3 1)) FALSE

§ `A2: the first day of a suspension and the three-year cap of s.10(a) (S10-12)`

-- s.10(a): suspend "for a period not exceeding three years".  A suspension that takes effect on 2026-05-01 and ends
-- on 2029-05-01 runs three years and one day if its first day is counted (ind-a's reading, asserted: it exceeds).
-- The encoding reads the cap with IL s.10(b), the first day being the event and not counted, so 2029-05-01 is the
-- last day allowed.  Both readings agree that 2029-04-30 is within and 2029-05-02 is not (asserted in
-- ind-a-tests-s10-s11.l4).
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` (`Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)` WITH `the measure` IS `suspend the licence`, `the grounds` IS (`Grounds under section 10(a)` WITH `the licence was granted on false, mistaken, misleading or partial information` IS TRUE, `a condition for the grant ceased to hold` IS FALSE, `the only condition that ceased to hold is a condition of section 6(a)(4)` IS FALSE, `the licensee breached a licence condition` IS FALSE, `the licensee breached a duty or prohibition under the Law or another enactment in connection with the activity as a licensee` IS FALSE, `the licensee gave false, misleading, mistaken or partial information when it was demanded` IS FALSE, `the licensee showed lack of professionalism or negligence that may endanger life or damage property` IS FALSE), `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE, `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE, `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE, `the period of the restriction or suspension` IS JUST (`Period of a restriction or suspension under section 10` WITH `begins on` IS YMD 2026 5 1, `ends on` IS JUST (YMD 2029 5 1)))
